milf.quest.magic_step_i.guardian_of_the_:
Use the <keyword>Runed Tablet</keyword> on the <keyword>Eldritch Lock</keyword> and the way to the boss hall opens. <warning>Something stirs beyond the door.</warning>

Each labyrinth is guarded by one of these:
- <curse>Eldritch Warden</curse>;
- <curse>Eldritch Golem</curse>;
- <curse>The Eldritch Hierophant</curse>;
- <blood>Greater Crimson Portal</blood>;
- <poison>Giant Taintacle</poison> with its swarm.

Defeat the guardian to conquer the labyrinth and claim its rewards - most guardians can also drop a <magic>Primordial Pearl</magic>. The quest counts when you (or your team) land the killing blow.

Place it <property>directly under</property> an <magic>aura node</magic>. It does several things at once:

- the node stops <wave>draining vis</wave> from other nodes and cannot be drained by them;
- an <warning><shake amplitude=0.3 frequency=1.0>unstable</shake></warning> node no longer loses its vis, and there is a tiny chance the instability goes away for good;
- a <soul>fading</soul> node has a very, very small chance to become a pale one.

The power comes from the node itself: its vis does not drop, but it refills from the aura at <warning>half speed</warning>. A <property>redstone signal</property> turns the stabilizer off.

milf.quest.magic_step_i.simple_reforging:
Gives any weapon, tool or armor piece <magic><wave>brand new affixes</wave></magic> - even an item that had none before.

<named>Slots:</named>
- <property>center</property> - the item to reforge;
- <property>top-left</property> - the <keyword>rarity material</keyword> of the rarity you want;
- <property>bottom-right</property> - <keyword>Sigils of Rebirth</keyword>, the fuel of reforging.

Like an Enchanting Table, it offers <positive>three choices</positive>. None is stronger by default - pick the one you like. The second and third need two and three times the levels and materials, but take only <property>2 and 3 levels</property> of experience.

