milf.quest.when_dungeons_arise.forger_cr:
A perfected <keyword>Forger's Gem</keyword>. Keep it in your inventory while working at an anvil:

- forging <positive>never damages</positive> the anvil;
- forging costs <property>half the experience</property>;
- put a tool in the left slot and an <property>undamaged copy</property> of the same tool in the right one - the result becomes <magic><pulse>unbreakable</pulse></magic>. This costs <warning>50 levels</warning>.

An unbreakable tool in your hands works as a <soul>Totem of Undying</soul>.

<curse>Relic:</curse> only bearers of the <blood>Seven Curses</blood> or the <named>Ring of Redemption</named> can use it.

milf.quest.when_dungeons_arise.forger_ge:
Keep it in your inventory while working at an <property>anvil</property>:

- forging costs <positive>half the experience</positive>;
- the anvil wears out more slowly;
- the result can come out <keyword>more durable</keyword>.

Also found in <property>dungeon, mineshaft and stronghold chests</property>.

milf.quest.when_dungeons_arise.redemptio:
An <keyword>Enigmatic Amulet</keyword> reforged with <magic>sacred light</magic>. It still summons an <soul>Extradimensional Vessel</soul> with your items and experience when you die.

On top of that:
- the stronger your <property>attack charge</property>, the less damage you take;
- you take <positive><pulse>no damage</pulse></positive> from creatures you have <property>not attacked</property> yet;
- bonus <nature>Luck</nature>, damage reduction and armor toughness.

<curse>Relic:</curse> only bearers of the <blood>Seven Curses</blood> or the <named>Ring of Redemption</named> can use it.
